comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-19T07:15:31.966Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing. Searched the tracker for release reliability, failure rate, scheduled and dispatcher terms, and read the never-refile registry. Neither gap belongs to an existing item:\n- pm-prrlce (open) owns trigger-origin attribution and the existence of a separate series per origin. Its acceptance criteria require the series to report attempts, failures and stages; they set no rate policy and do not say how a skipped run counts.\n- pm-0trehk (open) owns nightly re-shard lineage (warm-up for renamed legs). It covers nightly families only, not the release origin series.\n- pm-e70zh5 (closed) delivered the native-schedule rolling measure, and pm-44u3wt (closed) made the cron window and missing runs detectable. Both acceptance criteria required detection only, and both remain correct: the native schedule stays red by design.\n- pm-9url9h is the dispatcher decision; it keeps the native scheduled denominator unchanged, and this item leaves it unchanged too.\nThe nightly Node 24 Ubuntu leg's 10/30 failure rate is not filed: its failures cluster in 2026-10-24..31 and age out of the window."
body: ""
